    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by **Junior Caminero** (72.81) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (65.71). **Junior Caminero** remains our premier start, benefiting from a high-leverage spot in the two-hole against a vulnerable Alcantara; his combination of park factors and strong SP skill upside makes him our most efficient bet for counting stats. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** presents a compelling case despite the lower lineup slot; the combination of a high-value dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) and the necessary aggressive baserunning profile needed to tackle the scarcity of our SB category keeps him firmly in the elite tier, even with a minor efficiency penalty for facing an elite hold pitcher.\n\nStrategic lineup construction forced difficult decisions at the margins, most notably with **Hyeseong Kim** (48.21), who serves as our strongest bench piece. While **Hyeseong Kim** offers a solid floor, he ultimately lost out to the more favorable platoon splits and order positions of **Caleb Durbin** and **Chase Meidroth**. We are exercising caution with high-end assets like **Yordan Alvarez** (57.58) and **Trea Turner** (58.04); both are startable, but they face significant headwinds today against deGrom and Chandler, respectively. Specifically, the downward pressure from the elite SP skill of their opponents lowers their output expectations, though their raw talent remains too significant to bench.\n\nInvestors should monitor the risk profile associated with our OF group, specifically **Luke Raley** (62.16). While his projected score is strong, it is heavily reliant on his ability to exploit a slow delivery from Buehler for stolen base opportunities. Conversely, **Carson Benge** (52.31) remains a marginal start; he is fighting a significant platoon disadvantage (-9%) against Rod\u00f3n, and his value today is almost entirely derived from his leadoff placement. With **Colt Keith** and **Zac Veen** currently unavailable, we are leaning heavily on our depth to survive these challenging pitching matchups, particularly looking for **Gary Sanchez** and **Dillon Dingler** to provide secondary support behind the heart of our order.",
